;
; exports.def -- export table of GFSDK_Aftermath_Lib.x64.dll
;
; Ordinals 1, 2, 3, 4 and 8 are the ones the Ghidra listing shows next to the thunks at
; 0x5590, 0x5570, 0x5580, 0x5550 and 0x55A0.  The remaining four names slot into 5, 6, 7
; and 9, which is exactly what the linker assigns when a .def file lists every export
; without an explicit ordinal: MSVC numbers them in ASCII order of the *decorated* name.
; The full alphabetical sequence below reproduces the original table one for one.
;
; x64 has a single calling convention, so no name decoration is involved: the exported
; names are the plain C identifiers.  (A 32 bit build of the same sources would export
; _GFSDK_Aftermath_GetData and friends with __cdecl decoration, hence the explicit
; ordinals here -- they keep the table stable whatever the target.)
;
; No LIBRARY statement: the export directory's module name then comes from the linker's
; output name, which the project sets to GFSDK_Aftermath_Lib.x64.dll.
;
EXPORTS
    GFSDK_Aftermath_DX11_CreateContextHandle    @1
    GFSDK_Aftermath_DX11_Initialize             @2
    GFSDK_Aftermath_DX12_CreateContextHandle    @3
    GFSDK_Aftermath_DX12_Initialize             @4
    GFSDK_Aftermath_GetData                     @5
    GFSDK_Aftermath_GetDeviceStatus             @6
    GFSDK_Aftermath_GetPageFaultInformation     @7
    GFSDK_Aftermath_ReleaseContextHandle        @8
    GFSDK_Aftermath_SetEventMarker              @9
